; The integration check: does an instrumented build actually compile and
; register?
;
; [windtrap_mutate_forced] is preprocessed with the instrumenter
; directly, so every ordinary build type-checks the generated code -
; under every warning but 70 (missing .mli), all fatal. That is what
; caught the preamble's real hazard: Windtrap_runtime.Mutate spreads the site
; record's field names across three record types, so qualifying them
; (which is all coverage needs) still leaves warning 42.
;
; Its [shadowed] module is the emission law's regression test: it
; redefines every unqualified name a guard could reach, including the
; TYPE [bool], and therefore compiles only while every arm the
; instrumenter emits is Stdlib-qualified. Its [oracle] module is the
; population test_registration arms one mutant at a time, to check that
; each encoding MEANS the rewrite its report names - which no expansion
; golden can establish.
;
; [windtrap_mutate_stanza] carries the ordinary opt-in stanza instead, so
; it is inert without the flag and instrumented under
; [dune build --instrument-with ppx_windtrap.mutate] - which is what
; proves the backend is selectable by that name at all.

(library
 (name windtrap_mutate_forced)
 (modules forced no_guard oracle shadowed)
 (flags
  (:standard -w +a-70 -warn-error +a))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_windtrap.mutate)))

(library
 (name windtrap_mutate_stanza)
 (modules stanza)
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.mutate)))

; [windtrap_mutate_disambiguate] is the typing-context regression: its
; module compiles only while the guards type-check their lifted operands
; in source order, because every later record field in it resolves from
; the type a first, qualified access taught the checker. It is a library
; of its own, not a module of [forced], because it must keep dune's
; DEFAULT warning set: type-directed disambiguation is warning 40's
; subject, and the [-w +a] battery would reject the uninstrumented
; source itself. Preprocessed directly, like [forced], so the regression
; is a compile failure on every ordinary build.

(library
 (name windtrap_mutate_disambiguate)
 (modules disambiguate)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_windtrap.mutate)))

; Nothing links [windtrap_mutate_both]: its job is to be compiled with
; both backends enabled at once, which is the stanza pair the manual
; shows. Coverage wraps application out-edges, mutation replaces
; expressions with guards, and each must survive the other's output.

(library
 (name windtrap_mutate_both)
 (modules both)
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.coverage))
 (instrumentation
  (backend ppx_windtrap.mutate)))

(test
 (name test_registration)
 (modules test_registration)
 (libraries
  windtrap.runtime
  windtrap_mutate_forced
  windtrap_mutate_stanza
  windtrap_mutate_disambiguate))
